# Chase work loop (discuss → Opus → Grok)

When this Cursor chat is the Sume **main agent** with Chase, default to this
loop. Policy SoT (do not fork forever):  
`~/.agents/skills/sume-main-agent-orchestration/SKILL.md`  
§ "Chase work loop — discuss → lock → mega-issue → Opus → Grok".

Opus Shell recipe: `~/.cursor/rules/opus-background-terminal.mdc`.  
Graphite enqueue/land ops: `~/.agents/skills/sume-gt-mq/SKILL.md` (required
before any `gt submit` / `gt merge`).

## What this is

Chase and main **talk first** (intent, naming, defaults, non-goals), then main
**files a durable issue** and **hands implementation to Opus**. Main does not
silently become the sole implementer for work Chase expected on that flow.

## Roles

| Who | Owns |
|-----|------|
| Chase | Product locks, “go / defer / merge까지” |
| Main (this chat) | Discuss (match Chase’s language), survey, issue, launch workers, **self-contained chat report** (Slack is a mirror) |
| Opus | **Default author** if Chase did not name a model. BP → fresh clone → `gt submit` → `gt merge` (MQ) → **STOP** with `LANDED: no` / `NOT 완료` |
| Fable | Author **only** when Chase said Fable. Same enqueue path as Opus → **STOP** (`LANDED: no`) |
| Grok | **Always** MQ land babysit after Opus **or** Fable enqueue (`agent-human-stream --backend grok`) — **stay until `origin/main` `(#N)`**. Also author if Chase said Grok. Never Cursor `Task`. |
| Composer | Explore only |

**Default author = Opus.** **Default land owner = Grok** after Opus/Fable
enqueue. Only leave land on Opus/Fable when Chase said `merge까지` /
`landing까지` for that task.

## Step-by-step

### 1) Discuss
- Clarify outcome, surfaces (UI/docs/API), and what must *not* change.
- Light code/docs peeks OK; do not start a parallel full implementation.
- User-facing replies: **same language as Chase’s latest message** (usually Korean).

### 2) Lock
Capture in issue/BP, not chat memory only:
- Product nouns / defaults / wire vs chrome splits
- Non-goals and “Needs verification”
- Stage boundary: `STOP at MQ enqueue` vs `Opus owns land`
- Dev-only unless Chase authorizes prod

### 3) Mega-issue
- Prefer `/github-mega-issue` / `github-mega-issue` skill.
- Self-contained enough that Opus needs no prior transcript.
- Clear/small: main may write the issue. Heavy design: Opus may draft issue then implement (Pipeline 1).
- Create when Chase said to file / “그렇게 가보자” on that flow — not a silent draft-only unless they asked for a draft first.

### 4) Hand to Opus
Pick a **job slug** first (2–4 kebab tokens, aim for 3) — e.g.
`format-uifix-pdp`, `format-float-request`. Optional issue suffix only
(`…-2000`). Never `--name 2000` alone. Same stem for the prompt file and
Grok land prompt (`/tmp/sume-grok-prompts/<job-slug>.md`).

**Terminal + board title (required):** Shell `description` (and Active
workers board Job column) must be:

`Opus : <job-slug> (#<issue>)`

e.g. `Opus : dashboard-ui-chrome (#2819)`. Resume/steer keeps that exact
string. Never prose titles (“Create arch…”, “Relaunch dead…”). Details:
`opus-background-terminal.mdc` + `status-board.mdc` +
`active-workers-canvas.mdc` + `end-of-turn-worker-brief.mdc` +
`slack-coding-agents.mdc`.

```bash
cat > /tmp/sume-opus-prompts/<job-slug>.md <<'EOF'
Work in **English**.
Issue: <url>
Chase locks: …
Stage: BP → cstack-clone → implement → gt create → gt submit → cstack-gt-wait-merge → STOP with LANDED: no / NOT 완료 → cstack-clone-rm
HANDOFF: grok-land
Chase 완료 only after origin/main has (#N). Enqueue is not 완료.

Required skill: read ~/.agents/skills/sume-gt-mq/SKILL.md before any gt submit/merge.

GRAPHITE (hard lock):
- Isolated clone only: `CLONE="$(cstack-clone <job-slug>)"` then `cd "$CLONE"`.
  All `gt` commands run in that clone. Forbidden: `git worktree` under the
  shared Cursor checkout (#2383). Forbidden: `gh pr create` (single or stack).
  Publish ONLY via `gt submit`. If submit fails (trunk out of date): new
  `cstack-clone` → cherry-pick/track → `gt submit`. Never `gh pr create`.
- After `gt submit`: SAME session — `cstack-gt-wait-merge`
  (poll 5–12s, default 8s; `--rm <job-slug>` after enqueue).
  That binary is the ready-signal. Do NOT write a `sleep` + `grep` loop.
  Ready = ONLY `Your stack is ready to merge` or `(Ready to merge)` /
  `(Ready to merge as stack)`. Forbidden: substring grep `ready to merge`
  (false-matches `Cannot determine if stack is ready to merge` and
  `not ready to merge`). Failed CI / `Required checks failed` → binary
  exits 2 immediately — break, do NOT keep polling Ready.
  Already merging / already in the merge queue → exit 0 (STOP).
  Cannot determine → binary keeps waiting (do NOT `gt merge`).
- Repo CI flake: ≤2 `gh run rerun --failed`, then minimal CI unblock commit.
  Forbidden: endless rerun with no code change. Still blocked →
  `HANDOFF: grok-ci-merge`.
- Forbidden: ScheduleWakeup then exit before enqueue evidence.
  Stay in-session until enqueue confirmed (no minute cap).
- Own only this train. STOP immediately after enqueue.
  Done report: clone path + Graphite URL + GitHub PR URL + enqueue
  evidence + `LANDED: no` + `NOT 완료` + `HANDOFF: grok-land`.
  After enqueue: `cstack-clone-rm <job-slug>` (or `--rm` on the waiter)
  unless land still needs the tree.
EOF
cd <repo> && claude-human-stream --name <job-slug> "$(cat /tmp/sume-opus-prompts/<job-slug>.md)"
```
Shell: `block_until_ms: 0`, **`description`: `Opus : <job-slug> (#N)`**.
Never Cursor `Task` + `claude-opus-*`.

Prompt must include: issue URL, locks, **`sume-gt-mq` required-skill line**,
the **GRAPHITE hard-lock block** above (verbatim intent), no
`move_agent_to_root`, dev-only, done-report shape, handoff line. `gt` is
first-class like `gh` — never author with `gh pr create` on `sume-com`.

### 5) Tell Chase (short)
- Issue URL, title `Opus : <job-slug> (#N)`, `session_id=…`
- Do **not** poll; completion notification is the monitor

### 6) On Opus completion notification
1. Read `—— final ——` (+ `session_id`) only.
2. Brief status in Chase’s language.
3. If MQ enqueued (or PRs open) and land ≠ Opus: **launch Grok land babysit
   immediately** via `agent-human-stream --backend grok` (authorized by this
   loop — do not re-ask “머지할까요?”). Never Cursor `Task` / `cursor-grok-*`.
   **Do not tell Chase 완료** — enqueue is not landed.
4. Stack / PR → Graphite MQ. **Opus should already have enqueued** via
   `gt merge` (fallback label). Grok watches draft CI → **stays until**
   `origin/main` has `(#N)` (re-enqueue on eject; do not STOP at enqueue).
   Not GitHub `mergedAt` (Graphite FF often leaves `mergedAt: null` /
   state `CLOSED`). Do not thrash restack while Graphite says “already
   merging” / draft CI is running. If Opus used `HANDOFF: grok-ci-merge`,
   Grok does CI → label → stay until main tip.
5. Say **완료** to Chase only after that `origin/main` proof.

### 7) Residuals
Leave issue OPEN with an explicit residual, or close when AC met. Smoke/QA
workers: follow Chase constraints (e.g. **api.dev curl, not MCP** when said).

## Phrase triggers (run this loop)

- “mega-issue → opus”, “/github-mega-issue”, “BP → PR”, “플로우 타자”
- “그렇게 가보자” after a product lock discussion
- Naming / default / tone decisions that need a GitHub SoT before code

## Anti-patterns

| Bad | Do instead |
|-----|------------|
| Main implements the whole feature Chase meant for Opus | Issue → Opus |
| PR with no issue when mega-issue flow was requested | File issue first |
| Opus left babysitting land after MQ enqueue | Grok Shell land (`agent-human-stream --backend grok`) |
| Grok re-enqueues when Opus already queued | Watch draft / act only on failure |
| MCP “diagnosis” for Format/API smoke after Chase forbade it | `curl` api.dev |
| Re-ask merge after default handoff | Just launch Grok |
| Dump full Opus tool log into chat | `—— final ——` only |
| Issue-only worker names (`2000`, `issue-2000`) | Job slug first: `format-uifix-pdp` |
| Prose Shell titles (“Create arch…”, `Cursor (#…)`) | `description`: `Opus : <job-slug> (#N)` = board Job |
| Exit after ScheduleWakeup before enqueue | Stay in-session until enqueue evidence (`sume-gt-mq`) |
| `gh pr create` (any reason, incl. gt submit fail) | Fresh clone → `gt create` → `gt submit` |
| `gh pr checks` + sleep loops as CI wait | `cstack-gt-wait-merge` (5–12s) → `gt merge` |
| Dry-run sleep while `Required checks failed` | Break → ≤2 rerun / CI unblock / handoff (`sume-gt-mq`) |
| Endless `gh run rerun` on repo flake | ≤2 reruns → minimal CI unblock → or `HANDOFF: grok-ci-merge` |
| Default `sleep 20+` Ready wait | Cap **12s** (prefer 8s); use `cstack-gt-wait-merge` |
| `git worktree` under Cursor checkout + `gt` | `cstack-clone <slug>` |
| Grok clones / `gt track` just to merge | Label fallback only; prefer Opus `gt merge` |
| Enqueue unbound `gh`-only PR | Repair `gt submit` first, then enqueue |
| Habitual rebase / Update branch while in MQ | Wait for Graphite draft CI / restack |
| Treat Graphite FF `CLOSED`+`mergedAt:null` as not landed | Check `origin/main` `(#N)` |
| Tell Chase 완료 on enqueue / green CI / “Your changes” | 완료 only after `origin/main` `(#N)` |
| Land worker STOP at enqueue / `HANDOFF: grok-land` | Stay until main tip; re-enqueue on eject |
| Infinite “observe MQ” with no draft URL / no red | Report draft + act only on failure |

## Parallel trains

Multiple Opus job slugs OK. Note rebase risk when trains touch the same
paths. Keep Chase oriented with a short board (slug → issue → state → owner).
